how to log meals can feel overwhelming.","mistakenAssumption":"You need to stick to one method of logging for it to be effective.","lesson":"Offering multiple input methods can alleviate decision fatigue.","factIds":["cal-ai-methods"],"productMechanism":"Record food by meal photo, barcode scan or description.","practicalAction":"Try logging your next meal by taking a photo instead of manually entering it.","takeaway":"Experimenting with different logging methods can make tracking feel less daunting.","limitations":"Photo analysis accuracy may vary; ensure good conditions for best results."},{"slot":4,"problem":"The guilt of missing a log can overshadow healthy intentions.","mistakenAssumption":"You must log every calorie to be successful in weight management.","lesson":"Understanding that flexibility in logging can support a balanced approach.","factIds":["cal-ai-methods"],"productMechanism":"Record food by meal photo, barcode scan or description.","practicalAction":"If you forget to log a meal, focus on logging your next meal instead of stressing over the missed entry.","takeaway":"Flexibility in logging can help maintain a healthier mindset towards nutrition.","limitations":"The app does not guarantee exact calorie counts or health results."}]}

